logically equivalent to $A.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y∨(X∧Y) & ≡Y∨(Y∧X) \\\\  & ≡Y≢X.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :step/id #uuid "b0f2e79f-7c2d-591d-875f-4038c46d10e7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407273}}] :activity/title "The Absorption Laws" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407253}]}
